  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (basis cash); proprietary funds accrual (business_type measure net position, pp14-15), as FY2024. Governmental lines from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (pp8-11). Fund balance roll-forward: 600,538 + 697,545 - 977,065 + 209,556 - 0 - 28,604 = 501,970 (p11). Total column transfers in 209,556, out 0 (85,812 interfund eliminated in the Adjustments column). Grant Loan Advances (81,000) / Repayments 52,396 (Community Development Fund revolving loans) in other_financing, as FY2024. Business-type: 2,824,252 + 1,283,582 - 1,112,994 - 209,556 = 2,785,284. Grants: the budgetary comparison schedule (p18) prints Federal Receipts 209,505 = governmental Grants 198,187 + Sewer Grant Proceeds 11,318, so both are federal grants. Proprietary cash-flow statement (pp16-17) not recorded (proprietary is GAAP-only; as FY2024). Ending cash = governmental funds balance sheet Total column Cash in Bank 495,648 (p7); Cash at County Treasurer 13,822 printed separately; no prior-year cash printed, so beginning cash null. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (pp1-2), since it includes capital assets, loans and debt not on the governmental funds balance sheet (as FY2024). Detail: Schedule of Expenditures by fund (pp20-21; Keno Fund all zero); the total-primary-government budget schedule (pp18-19) combines governmental and business-type revenues and its governmental disbursement lines duplicate the expenditure schedule, so only its four business-type disbursement lines are recorded (no per-fund printed totals for them), as FY2024. Read pages 1-22 of 22"
